//? Title: Lempel–Ziv–Welch integer-code compression
//? Subtitle: Actual streaming dictionary learning, special-case decoding and the original classic code stream
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
LZW begins with256 one-byte dictionary words and learns longer phrases while
emitting integer codes. The decoder reconstructs those phrases from the codes,
including one special missing-code case. We retain the original classic and
repeated-pangram fixtures, expose actual producing decisions, reject corrupt
code streams, and distinguish integer-code counts from packed compressed bytes.
)

\toc

> Tiny streaming example: AAA

The initial dictionary contains every one-byte word at its unsigned byte code.
The encoder holds a pending word w. For each actual next byte c, look up w+c. If
present, keep the longer pending word; otherwise emit w’s code, learn w+c at the
next free integer code, and reset the pending word to c. At end, emit any
remaining pending word.

For AAA, the first A is already known. The second byte makes unknown AA: emit65,
learn AA as256, and keep A pending. The third byte extends that pending A to the
now-known AA, which is finally flushed as256. The real output is[65,256]. The
diagram and decision table use the actual producing trace; they do not rebuild a
second dictionary for display.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lzw_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/lzw.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::lzw_encode_trace("AAA");
    std::print("| actual input index | actual final flush | actual prior prefix | actual candidate | known " "| actual emitted code or minus1 | actual learned code or minus1 |\n| ---: | --- | --- | --- " "| --- | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &s : t.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.input_index,
                   s.flush, s.prefix, s.candidate, s.known, s.emitted_code,
                   s.learned_code);
    auto &learn = t.steps[1];
    auto &flush = t.steps.back();
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("lookup", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual unknown candidate\n{}", learn.candidate)).node(
        "learn", {6, 0},
        std::format("Actual emit{}, learn{}\nword{}", learn.emitted_code,
                    learn.learned_code, learn.candidate)).node(
        "flush", {12, 0},
        std::format("Actual final flush code{}\nword{}", flush.emitted_code,
                    flush.prefix)).edge("lookup", "learn").edge("learn", "flush");
    d.save_svg("build/lzw_tiny.svg");
}
```
