> Original classic and repeated-pangram streams

Retain TOBEORNOTTOBEORTOBEORNOT,24 bytes, with original16-code
stream84,79,66,69,79,82,78,79,84,256,258,260,265,259,261,263. The native helper
owns that exact classic input. Codes0..255 denote seeded single bytes; larger
codes refer to phrases learned by the producing encoder. A separate shared
native fixture retains the original89-byte repeated pangram and its65 emitted
codes. Both are decoded and compared exactly with their input bytes.

The figure plots the actual emitted integer codes of the classic stream.
Neither16 codes for24 bytes nor65 codes for89 bytes is a compressed-byte ratio.
This API defines no bit packing, variable code-width schedule, dictionary reset,
clear/end codes or file framing, and is not a ready-to-use GIF/TIFF/compress
wire format. These exact synthetic fixtures need no external dataset.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lzw_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/lzw.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/lz77.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto classic = dm::algorithms::lzw_classic_text();
    auto a = dm::algorithms::lzw_encode_analyze(classic);
    auto text = dm::algorithms::lz77_demo_text();
    auto other = dm::algorithms::lzw_encode_analyze(text);
    std::print("Actual classic input {}; input bytes {}; integer codes {}; exact round trip {}. Original " "longer input bytes {}; actual codes {}; exact round trip {}.\n\n| actual emitted code index " "| actual integer code | refers to learned phrase |\n| ---: | ---: | --- |\n",
               classic, classic.size(), a.codes.size(),
               dm::algorithms::lzw_decode(a.codes) == classic, text.size(),
               other.codes.size(),
               dm::algorithms::lzw_decode(other.codes) == text);
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < a.codes.size(); ++i) {
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", i, a.codes[i], a.codes[i] >= 256);
        x.push_back(i);
        y.push_back(a.codes[i]);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "actual integer code", {37, 99, 235}, 6).y_limits(0, 350).title("Original classic24-byte stream: actual16 emitted codes").x_label("actual emitted code index").y_label("actual native integer code").save_svg("build/lzw_original.svg");
}
