> Why a code equal to the next free code can be decoded

After decoding the current word, the decoder learns the previous word followed
by the current word’s first byte. It is therefore one learned entry behind the
encoder when the encoder emits a newly formed repeated word. If the supplied
code is exactly the next free dictionary code, the only consistent word is
previous+previous.first. This requires a nonempty previous word, guaranteed by a
valid seeded first code and induction on valid entries.

The hand-checkable stream[65,256,257,258] reconstructs A, AA, AAA, AAAA,
producing ten A bytes. Each of its final three codes is the actual next-code
special case. The native trace stores every actual decoded word, learned entry
and appended output span. A code beyond the next free code is corrupt, not
another version of this exception.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lzw_special.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/lzw.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::lzw_decode_trace({65, 256, 257, 258});
    std::print("| actual input code index | supplied code | actual special case | actual decoded word | " "actual learned code or minus1 | actual learned word | actual output begin | actual output " "end |\n| ---: | ---: | --- | --- | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: |\n");
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    for (auto &s : t.steps) {
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.input_index,
                   s.code, s.special, s.entry, s.learned_code, s.learned_entry,
                   s.output_begin, s.output_end);
        x.push_back(s.input_index);
        y.push_back(s.entry.size());
    }
    std::print("\nActual decoded text {}; actual bytes {}; actual special cases {}; actual conceptual " "dictionary bytes {}.\n",
               t.analysis.data, t.analysis.work.emitted_bytes,
               t.analysis.work.special_cases, t.analysis.work.dictionary_bytes);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "actual decoded length", {37, 99, 235}, 6).y_limits(0, 6).title("Actual next-free-code word reconstruction").x_label("actual input code index").y_label("actual decoded word length in bytes").save_svg("build/lzw_special.svg");
}
