> Verification and references

Native tests exhaust all1023 binary words through length nine against an
independent longest-current-phrase dictionary enumeration, verify actual
emitted/learned decisions and decoder source spans, and retain the exact
classic16-code and repeated-pangram65-code fixtures. Next-code special cases,
all256 byte values,200 arbitrary-byte inputs, complete invalid-code guards,
integer geometry, exact output/capture limits, empty cases and ownership are
covered. The ten-report batch passes 95 CTest cases, 30 directly instrumented
ASan/UBSan cases, 121 compiled and executed public examples, 601/601 scoped
documentation definitions and 11 representative hovers. Independent integer,
Fraction, graph, string and NumPy references verify 82,729 records, including
the complete original seeded LSH study. Frozen comparisons preserve ordinary
legacy results; malformed-input, sentinel-collision, ownership and
explicit-budget corrections are documented above. Thirteen checkout headers and
thirteen installed headers compile independently, and an installed-header native
consumer links and runs. Each complete report program runs against the checkout
library; all four native figures are reviewed and HTML/Markdown exports preserve
computed results and image bytes. Batch receipts:
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-214-223/`.

T. A. Welch(1984),
[A Technique for High-Performance Data Compression|https://doi.org/10.1109/MC.1984.1659158],
Computer17(6),8–19. Its dictionary-learning idea motivates this byte-seeded
integer-code implementation; packed formats, code-width schedules and reset
policies must be specified separately before making file-format or
compressed-byte claims.
